            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-11940-libpython3.12-minimal",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-11940 medium vulnerability for libpython3.12-minimal package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "tarfile.extractall() with the 'data' or 'tar'\n filter could be bypassed by a crafted archive where a hardlink \nreferences a symlink stored at a deeper name than the hardlink itself.  \nThe extraction fallback validated the symlink at it's archived location \nbut recreated it at the hardlink's shallower\npath, letting a relative\n target the filter judged contained escape the destination directory.  \nThis allowed a malicious tar archive to create a symlink pointing \noutside the destination, enabling out-of-destination file reads or \nwrites. This was an incomplete fix of CVE-2025-4330."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-11940",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-11940\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libpython3.12-minimal\nVersion: 3.12.3-1ubuntu0.16\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/info/libpython3.12-minimal:amd64.conffiles\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-11940](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-11940)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-11940**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libpython3.12-minimal  | 3.12.3-1ubuntu0.16  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/info/libpython3.12-minimal:amd64.conffiles  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-11940](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-11940)  |\n"
              },
