            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-15534-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-15534 medium vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Perl versions through 5.45.1 have out-of-bounds heap reads and writes during regular expression matching via an undersized superlinear cache in S_regmatch.\n\nThe regex engine's superlinear cache holds one bit per subject position for each participating WHILEM node, so the bit count is the subject length plus one times the number of nodes. Nothing checks that product for positive overflow of the signed 32-bit count: a 286331153 byte subject matched against a pattern with 15 participating nodes stores the count as 14, leaving a two byte cache. The cache is then indexed from the real match position and node number, so reads go past the end of the allocation, and on failure CACHEsayNO sets a bit past it.\n\nA caller that matches an attacker controlled subject of this size against a pattern of this shape can crash the process or corrupt heap memory."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-15534",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-15534\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.4\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/info/perl-base.list\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-15534](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-15534)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-15534**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | perl-base  | 5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.4  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/info/perl-base.list  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-15534](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-15534)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/perl-base@5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.4?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.7"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-84366-libpython3.12-minimal",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-84366 medium vulnerability for libpython3.12-minimal package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Scrapy is a high-level web crawling and scraping framework for Python. Prior to 2.17.0, in scrapy/core/downloader/handlers/s3.py, Scrapy's S3DownloadHandler converts an S3-scheme bucket and key request into a plaintext HTTP request to the corresponding S3 endpoint unless request.meta[\"is_secure\"] is explicitly enabled, then signs and sends the plaintext request with configured AWS credentials. A network attacker who can observe traffic between Scrapy and S3 can read the bucket and key path, AWS Authorization header, X-Amz-Security-Token when temporary credentials are used, S3 object contents, and S3 response headers. An active man-in-the-middle attacker can also modify the plaintext S3 response body, status code, and headers before Scrapy processes them, causing scraped-data poisoning, poisoned exports, HTTP cache poisoning when caching is enabled, or influence over later crawl targets through forged redirects or attacker-controlled links. Users making S3-scheme requests with AWS credentials are affected. This issue is fixed in version 2.17.0."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-84366",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-84366\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libpython3.12-minimal\nVersion: 3.12.3-1ubuntu0.16\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/info/libpython3.12-minimal:amd64.conffiles\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-84366](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-84366)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-84366**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libpython3.12-minimal  | 3.12.3-1ubuntu0.16  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/info/libpython3.12-minimal:amd64.conffiles  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-84366](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-84366)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/libpython3.12-minimal@3.12.3-1ubuntu0.16?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=python3.12"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.4"
              }
